# 0305 = 0304 plus the TX watchdog progress init.  Defaults change only
# the watchdog policy.
#
# Root cause found 2026-11-16: ruby_tx_progress_ms is only set at drain and
# is still 0 after boot, so the first prepared packet satisfied the 200 ms
# grace immediately and TXRESET (stop + FLUSHFIFO + ring reset) fired on the
# next 1 ms tick.  That destroyed the first echo before the host read and
# invalidated every 0304 arm (all shared the txreset=1 base cmdline).
# A/B evidence: Dpoll image with ruby_txreset=0 passes 512x5 + 1024x3 (8/8,
# no clear_halt, no TXRESET); the same image with txreset=1 fails the first
# read with USBError(-9).  The device never set TX_SENTSTALL.
#
# code (patches/0305-ruby-usb-txwatch-progress.patch):
#   ruby_tx_progress_ms = ruby_ms at the enqueue (ruby_inflight++);
#   banner content gate "RUBY USB: 0305 txwatch progress-init".
# patchset: 84f02bf95309987566fbe3c5c36a325dbcb0b9b55c14436ee354a35756aed01e
#           (288 files, computed locally from baseline-mirror)
#
# default cmdline (config/0305-boot.cmdline): ruby_txreset=0; the watchdog is
# opt-in again (vendor/mainline/U-Boot have no runtime TX recovery).  A
# zero-build arm with ruby_txreset=1 validates the fix: the first packet must
# now survive (no TXRESET before the read).
#
# arms: A default (txreset=0) -> native Windows 8/8;
#       B zero-build txreset=1  -> first write/read must match.
